---
const title = 'SEEING.md — The Perception Layer for AI';
const description =
  'An open perception specification that helps people and AI surface consequential assumptions before they become decisions at scale.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#11110f" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://seeing.md/" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://seeing.md/" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="SEEING.md home">SEEING<span>.md</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="#why">Why</a>
        <a href="#case">Case</a>
        <a href="#use">Use it</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">An open perception specification</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">AI scales the seeing that shaped it.</h1>
          <p class="hero-deck">
            SEEING.md helps people and AI surface consequential assumptions before
            they become decisions, systems, and actions at scale.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/SEEING.md" download>Download SEEING.md</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/billfoxco/seeing-md">View on GitHub</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sequence" aria-label="Seeing leads to intent, system, and scale">
          <span>Seeing</span>
          <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Intent</span>
          <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>System</span>
          <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Scale</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="statement" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
        <p class="section-number">01 / The missing layer</p>
        <h2 id="why-title">
          We are trying to align AI with human intent without examining what
          shaped the intent.
        </h2>
        <div class="statement-body">
          <p>
            Before a system is designed, trained, evaluated, prompted, or
            deployed, people have already decided what matters, what the problem
            is, what should be measured, and what a good outcome looks like.
          </p>
          <p>
            Most of those decisions do not feel like decisions. They feel like
            reality. SEEING.md introduces a pause before that invisible choice
            becomes machine-scale action.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="outcomes" aria-labelledby="outcomes-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-number">02 / What it changes</p>
          <h2 id="outcomes-title">A better-timed interruption.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="outcome-list">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Separate</h3>
            <p>Distinguish what is known from what has already been interpreted.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Surface</h3>
            <p>Make consequential assumptions visible before they become direction.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Ask</h3>
            <p>Pause for one clear question when missing meaning could change the action.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case" id="case" aria-labelledby="case-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-number">03 / One ordinary case</p>
          <h2 id="case-title">The answer was not where the risk began.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="case-grid">
          <article class="case-panel">
            <p class="case-label">The request</p>
            <blockquote>
              Assess the risk presented by this candidate’s employment gap.
            </blockquote>
            <p>
              The gap is a fact. The risk is already an interpretation. A fluent
              answer can carry both forward as though they were the same.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="case-panel case-panel-accent">
            <p class="case-label">With SEEING.md</p>
            <blockquote>
              You’ve described the employment gap as a risk. Should I first
              examine whether the gap is relevant, or assess it using your
              existing criteria?
            </blockquote>
            <p>
              The system does not declare the framing wrong. It makes the unseen
              choice visible and returns agency to the human.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="scope" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-number">04 / Its place in AI safety</p>
          <h2 id="scope-title">Upstream, not all-encompassing.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="scope-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>What it addresses</h3>
            <p>
              The human assumptions that enter a system through its purpose,
              data, measures, prompts, evaluation, and use—and can become more
              consequential as the system scales.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>What it does not</h3>
            <p>
              It does not prevent autonomous behavior, malicious use,
              cyberattacks, deception, or loss of control. Those risks require
              technical, organizational, and public safeguards of their own.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="use" id="use" aria-labelledby="use-title">
        <p class="section-number">05 / Begin</p>
        <h2 id="use-title">One file. One question further upstream.</h2>
        <p class="use-intro">
          Place SEEING.md in a project. Name it in the instructions your AI
          system reads. Apply it when judgment, people, strategy,
          interpretation, or consequential decisions are involved.
        </p>

        <div class="instruction">
          <p class="case-label">Suggested project instruction</p>
          <p>
            Before work involving judgment, people, strategy, interpretation,
            or consequential decisions, read SEEING.md. Use it to examine the
            framing and surface relevant assumptions before acting. Apply it
            proportionally; do not slow straightforward technical work
            unnecessarily.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary button-light" href="/SEEING.md" download>Download version 0.1.0</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/billfoxco/seeing-md">Test it. Question it. Help refine it. <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="origin" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
        <p class="section-number">Origin</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="origin-title">The file is open. The practice is relational.</h2>
          <p>
            SEEING.md emerged primarily from Bill Fox’s book,
            <em>The Perception Miracle</em>, and more than 500 explorations into
            how the mind’s past enters the present. The Perception Space is where
            that inquiry becomes an ongoing human practice through images,
            stillness, inquiry, and conversation.
          </p>
          <p>
            Its form was influenced by Brian Gardner’s exploration of DESIGN.md
            as a way to make the intent behind a design system legible to AI.
            SEEING.md carries the inquiry one level further upstream.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link dark-link" href="https://seedifferent.xyz">Explore SEE DIFFERENT <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">SEEING<span>.md</span></a>
      <p>Seeing is the first decision.</p>
      <a href="mailto:hello@seeing.md">hello@seeing.md</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --ink: #11110f;
    --paper: #f0eee8;
    --muted: #a9a69d;
    --line-dark: #35342f;
    --line-light: #d2cfc6;
    --amber: #b97616;
    --content: 1240px;
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .site-header,
  .hero,
  main > section,
  footer {
    padding-inline: max(24px, calc((100vw - var(--content)) / 2));
  }

  .site-header {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 2;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    display: flex;
    width: 100%;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding-block: 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(240, 238, 232, 0.18);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .wordmark {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 760;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .wordmark span {
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 30px;
  }

  nav a,
  footer a {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  nav a {
    color: rgba(240, 238, 232, 0.72);
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    min-height: 100svh;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr auto;
    padding-top: 150px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 1000px;
    align-self: center;
    padding-block: 60px 100px;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-number,
  .case-label {
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    color: var(--amber);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 730;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 970px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 8vw, 7.8rem);
    font-weight: 540;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 0.94;
  }

  .hero-deck {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 42px 0 0;
    color: rgba(240, 238, 232, 0.7);
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 18px;
    margin-top: 42px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 52px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 13px 22px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(240, 238, 232, 0.34);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 680;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    transition: background 160ms ease, color 160ms ease, border-color 160ms ease;
  }

  .button-primary {
    border-color: var(--paper);
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .button-secondary {
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .button:hover,
  .button:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--amber);
    background: var(--amber);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sequence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 22px;
    padding-top: 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
    color: rgba(240, 238, 232, 0.65);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .sequence span:first-child {
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .sequence i {
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--amber);
  }

  main > section:not(.hero) {
    padding-block: clamp(90px, 12vw, 170px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .statement {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 0.35fr) 1.65fr;
    gap: 60px;
  }

  .statement h2,
  .section-heading h2,
  .use h2,
  .origin h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    font-weight: 520;
    letter-spacing: -0.052em;
    line-height: 1.02;
  }

  .statement h2 {
    max-width: 1020px;
  }

  .statement-body {
    grid-column: 2;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 48px;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-top: 38px;
  }

  .statement-body p,
  .scope-grid p,
  .origin p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #4e4c46;
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 0.35fr) 1.65fr;
    gap: 60px;
    margin-bottom: 72px;
  }

  .outcome-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .outcome-list article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(70px, 0.35fr) 0.65fr 1fr;
    gap: 30px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: 30px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-light);
  }

  .outcome-list span {
    color: var(--amber);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }

  .outcome-list h3,
  .scope-grid h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    font-weight: 680;
  }

  .outcome-list p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #595750;
  }

  .case {
    background: #e7e4dc;
  }

  .case-grid,
  .scope-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .case-panel {
    padding: clamp(30px, 5vw, 64px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-light);
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  .case-panel + .case-panel {
    border-left: 0;
  }

  .case-panel-accent {
    border-top: 3px solid var(--amber);
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2.45rem);
    font-weight: 520;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.22;
  }

  .case-panel > p:last-child {
    margin: 44px 0 0;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-light);
    color: #5a5851;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .scope {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .scope .section-heading,
  .scope-grid {
    border-color: var(--line-dark);
  }

  .scope-grid {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
  }

  .scope-grid > div {
    padding: 48px 56px 0 0;
  }

  .scope-grid > div + div {
    padding-left: 56px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
  }

  .scope-grid p {
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: rgba(240, 238, 232, 0.62);
  }

  .use {
    background: var(--amber);
  }

  .use .section-number {
    color: rgba(17, 17, 15, 0.62);
  }

  .use h2 {
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .use-intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 36px 0 0;
    font-size: 1.18rem;
  }

  .instruction {
    max-width: 920px;
    margin-top: 64px;
    padding: 32px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ink);
    background: rgba(240, 238, 232, 0.15);
  }

  .instruction .case-label {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    color: rgba(17, 17, 15, 0.62);
  }

  .instruction p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .button-light {
    border-color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .text-link {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 15, 0.6);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 680;
  }

  .text-link span {
    margin-left: 8px;
  }

  .origin {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(170px, 0.35fr) 1.65fr;
    gap: 60px;
  }

  .origin > div {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .origin p {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .dark-link {
    margin-top: 34px;
  }

  footer {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding-block: 34px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  footer p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
  }

  footer > a:last-child {
    justify-self: end;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  :focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--amber);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    body {
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    nav {
      display: none;
    }

    .hero {
      min-height: auto;
      padding-top: 120px;
    }

    .hero-copy {
      padding-block: 70px 90px;
    }

    .sequence {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 11px;
    }

    .sequence i {
      width: 1px;
      height: 18px;
      margin-left: 4px;
    }

    .statement,
    .section-heading,
    .origin {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .statement-body {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .section-heading {
      margin-bottom: 44px;
    }

    .outcome-list article {
      grid-template-columns: 44px 1fr;
    }

    .outcome-list p {
      grid-column: 2;
    }

    .case-grid,
    .scope-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .case-panel + .case-panel {
      border-top: 0;
      border-left: 1px solid var(--line-light);
    }

    .case-panel-accent {
      border-top: 3px solid var(--amber) !important;
    }

    .scope-grid > div,
    .scope-grid > div + div {
      padding: 34px 0;
      border-left: 0;
    }

    .scope-grid > div + div {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
    }

    footer {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    footer > a:last-child {
      justify-self: start;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    html {
      scroll-behavior: auto;
    }

    *,
    *::before,
    *::after {
      transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    }
  }
</style>
